.TH "LINTO-BIBLIO" 1

.SH "BibTeX and bibliography tools"
.PP
The \fBbiblio\fP group contains utilities for converting and formatting BibTeX,
JSON, Markdown, and YAML data\. Use \fBlinto help biblio\fP to see its current
commands\. Typical tasks include:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto biblio bib2json \-\-help
linto biblio json2bib \-\-help
linto biblio bib\-order\-props \-\-help
linto bibyml2bib \-\-help
linto biblio csv2qmd \-\-help
linto biblio md2json \-\-help
linto bib2dirbibs \-\-help
linto biblio qmd2yml \-\-help
linto yml\-renumber \-\-help
.fi
.RE
.PP
Many tools expect to run from the project directory containing the relevant
\fB\.bib\fP, \fB\.qmd\fP, JSON, Markdown, or YAML files\. Check each command's \fB\-\-help\fP for
its exact arguments and whether it writes files in place\. Back up important
bibliography data before using tools that modify it\.

.SS "Build BibTeX files from a YAML mapping"
.PP
\fBlinto bibyml2bib\fP selects entries from a BibTeX file using a YAML mapping of
citation keys to numbers\. Pass the BibTeX file first and the YAML file second:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto bibyml2bib biblio\.bib biblio\.yml
.fi
.RE
.PP
The YAML should contain only string keys and numeric values, for example:
.RS
.PP
.nf
"ref\-one": 1
"ref\-two": 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
By default, the output is \fBbiblio\-numbered\.bib\fP; use \fB\-o FILE\fP or
\fB\-\-output\-file FILE\fP to choose another output path\. Entries are written in YAML
order with their \fBnumber\fP field set to the mapped value\. Missing keys are
reported and skipped\. Calling \fBlinto bibyml2bib\fP with no arguments retains the
legacy batch mode for \fB_pieces\-*\.yml\fP files and \fBfr\.bib\fP\.

.SS "Build a numbered references YAML from citations"
.PP
\fBlinto biblio qmd2yml FILE\.qmd\fP extracts unique Pandoc\-style citation keys and
writes a numbered YAML mapping\. Use \fB\-y\fP/\fB\-\-yml\fP to extend an existing mapping:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto biblio qmd2yml \-\-yml references\.yml report\.qmd
.fi
.RE
.PP
The existing YAML is emitted first with empty lines removed\. Keys already
present in it are skipped; new keys are appended in citation order, numbered
from one greater than the last mapping value\. Use \fB\-\-order\-by key\fP to sort the
new keys, or \fB\-\-format csv\fP when you do not need to extend a YAML file\. With no
\fB\-\-yml\fP input, \fB\-\-start NUMBER\fP sets the first YAML number\.
